%U A400908 35,51,26,106,53,45,140,57,57,59,118,122,61,63,42,80,33,67,134,102,105,71,284
%N A400908 Minimum of gcd(binomial(n,i), binomial(n,j)) over all pairs (i,j) with 2 <= i <= j <= floor(n/2).
%C A400908 Erdős Problem 698 considers pairs with 2 <= i < j <= floor(n/2), while Bergman's Theorem 2 allows i = j. The two minima agree for n >= 6; with i = j allowed, the sequence can start at n = 4, where a(4) = binomial(4,2) = 6 and a(5) = binomial(5,2) = 10.
%H A400908 Seiichi Manyama, <a href="/A400908/b400908.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 4..10000</a>
%H A400908 George M. Bergman, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/0806.0607">On common divisors of multinomial coefficients</a>, arXiv:0806.0607 [math.NT], 2008; see Section 2, Theorem 2.
%H A400908 T. F. Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/698">Erdős Problem 698</a>.
